{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CUTOVER IS LIVE, AND THE INDUCED-VOTER_ERROR DRILL LANDED ON THE ANTHROPIC PATH AFTER ALL. I nearly recorded the opposite; the timeline below is the evidence that settled it, and I am recording the reasoning because a single ambiguous reading would have produced a false claim in either direction.\n\nEXACT TIMELINE, from the autodeploy unit journal and the usage log rather than from inference:\n  00:01:33Z  autodeploy sees target 5892134975 (the flip) and DEFERS: reason review-in-flight\n  00:03:43Z  AUTODEPLOY_REVIEW_INTERRUPT {\"reason\": \"bound-exceeded\"} — the 1800s deferral bound expired, so the deploy proceeded anyway; 'review-bot sources or secrets changed; sync + refresh .env + rebuild'\n  00:04:03Z  the NEW container is created (build starts; the OLD container is still serving and draining)\n  00:05:50Z  drill baseline: voter_error_count=209, alarm rebar-gerrit-voter-errors OK (last state change Aug 2 16:17)\n  00:05:51Z  INDUCE: '127.0.0.1 gerrit' appended to /etc/hosts in the SERVING container; reachability proof from inside it: http_code=000, curl exit 7 (failed to connect)\n  00:11:14Z  EIGHT VOTER_ERROR markers (count 209 -> 217)\n  00:11:27Z  'review-bot redeployed + healthy' — the swap to the new container COMPLETES here\n  00:12:47Z  ALARM: rebar-gerrit-voter-errors OK -> ALARM\n  00:13:12Z  FIRST Bedrock call anywhere in the usage log\n  00:14:26Z  RESTORE: override removed, reachability re-proven from inside the container: http_code=200\n\nWHY THIS PROVES THE DRILL WAS ON THE ANTHROPIC PATH. The VOTER_ERRORs at 00:11:14 precede the 'redeployed + healthy' swap at 00:11:27 by 13 seconds, and the usage log's FIRST bedrock: call is 00:13:12 — so no Bedrock call had occurred anywhere on the box when the markers fired. The container serving at 00:05:51 also reported the class slots UNSET via printenv, and that reading is trustworthy here rather than an artifact because the same exec in the same command successfully wrote /etc/hosts and returned a reachability result: exec was working, so 'unset' was a real answer and not a swallowed failure. I had flagged the opposite risk (that '|| echo SLOTS_NOTSET' could mask an exec failure during recreation) and this is what rules it out.\n\nTHE MECHANISM, and it is a tidier story than the one I pre-registered. All eight failures are at the DEDUP CHECK, not the vote POST:\n    VOTER_ERROR {\"change_id\": \"Ia9efcabefc293279fb710c181a697ed00c20cffa\", \"vote_value\": null, \"http_status\": null,\n                 \"error\": \"has_llm_review_vote: GET /a/changes/.../review transport error: [Errno 11...\"}\n    VOTER_ERROR {\"change_id\": \"I58a7822723d10d0fe0c964bdedddbb7b0ae30887\", \"vote_value\": null, ...}\nSo: the deploy's shutdown drain flushed the queued webhooks; each queued review entered review_and_vote, hit has_llm_review_vote FIRST, got a refused connection wrapped as GerritError by gerrit_client.py:116, and fired _voter_error at voter.py:470 — exactly the site I pre-registered. EVERY ONE has vote_value: null, so NO VOTE WAS CAST and no false +1 or -1 was possible, and all eight cost ZERO LLM tokens because the failure precedes the adapter. The affected changes belong to other sessions and are left vote-LESS, which is the recoverable state by design: the backfill reconciler re-drives vote-less changes on its interval.\n\nTHE ALARM CHAIN, END TO END ON LIVE TRAFFIC. rebar/host:voter_errors published 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 and then 12.0; the alarm moved OK -> ALARM at 00:12:47Z with reason 'Threshold Crossed: 1 datapoint [4.0 (04/08/26 00:07:00)] was greater than the threshold (0.0)'. So the whole path is proven: _voter_error -> stderr/journald marker -> observability.sh section 4 grep -> rebar/host:voter_errors -> the S4b alarm. The induction method was registered on this ticket BEFORE execution, which is what the criterion asks for, and the observed timestamps are above.\n\nBONUS VALIDATION I DID NOT PLAN. AUTODEPLOY_REVIEW_INTERRUPT fired for real at 00:03:43 with reason 'bound-exceeded' — so bug 34cd's marker, and the rebar-autodeploy-review-interrupts alarm I applied earlier today, have now both been exercised by live traffic rather than by inspection.\n\nTHE CUTOVER, VERIFIED INSIDE THE RUNNING CONTAINER:\n    REBAR_LLM_FRONTIER_MODEL = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n    REBAR_LLM_STANDARD_MODEL = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n    REBAR_LLM_TRIVIAL_MODEL  = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\n    REBAR_LLM_MODEL          = None\n    REBAR_USAGE_LOG          = /var/gerrit/site/reviewbot/usage.jsonl\n  rebar's own resolution in that container: frontier/standard/trivial -> the three bedrock: profiles.\n  'from pydantic_ai.providers.bedrock import BedrockProvider' -> SYMBOL_OK in the REBUILT image.\n\nTHE PER-CALL TALLY — every clause of the usage-log criterion, each as an observed figure rather than asserted collectively. 8 records in /var/gerrit/site/reviewbot/usage.jsonl:\n    00:13:12  bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8                  in=430479 out=5915 cache_read=386204  code-review-base\n    00:14:30  bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8                  in=334637 out=5133 cache_read=308003  code-review-tests\n    00:15:15  bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8                  in=181367 out=2918 cache_read=149162  code-review-scope-intent\n    00:15:20  bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8                  in=10459  out=200  cache_read=0       code-review-project-review-phase-boundaries\n    00:15:21  bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6                in=11367  out=9    cache_read=0       code-review-verify\n    00:15:22  bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6                in=7207   out=8    cache_read=0       code-review-coach\n    00:16:31  bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0   in=1745   out=345  cache_read=0       ticket-digest\n    00:16:41  bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0   in=1779   out=357  cache_read=0       ticket-digest\n  * EVERY call is on a bedrock:us.anthropic.* inference profile — 8 of 8.\n  * ZERO direct-Anthropic calls — no 'anthropic:' model appears in any record.\n  * The FRONTIER class resolves to the OPUS profile (code-review-base / tests / scope-intent).\n  * The STANDARD class resolves to the SONNET profile (code-review-verify / code-review-coach) — the per-pass split observed IN PRODUCTION, not just in config.\n  * NONZERO cache_read_tokens: 386204, 308003 and 149162 on the three large frontier calls. Bedrock prompt caching is engaging on the inference profiles, as [rebar:2932-8a98-6d70-4550] measured.\n  * The trivial class also resolved and invoked (haiku profile, ticket-digest), which the criteria did not require.\nThis is the direct, positive proof that the Anthropic path is UNUSED, which is what the plan wanted rather than the withdrawn 'no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the container' criterion — the credential is still present by design and the tally shows it is not being used."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785802790214096001,"uuid":"4aa30b56-e707-45ca-9d6b-92b166e8d111"}